Backport: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/commit/3ba0a0b23761ef8209827f7f3dd0f82713c33bbe
Upstream PR #160297 (v2026.9.7): fix: recheck unfinished plans before an agent stops.
Also carries the progress_card description sentence from upstream PR #162903
(b0632d0effc5d0d4aba5d4caa54ba2424b641751, v2026.10.1).

A run can save an unfinished progress_card plan and then end with an ordinary
visible reply ("I will continue with the rest"). v2026.8.1 treats that reply
as the end of the turn, so the desktop card stays on "step 3/10 · turn ended"
and nothing resumes the work. Upstream gives such a run one hidden, same-prompt
completion check. The model continues feasible work, reconciles the plan, or
reports the concrete limitation. The check runs at most once per run, keeps
completed tool results and replays nothing. Old cards, cancelled, timed-out,
yielded, refused or length-limited runs, queued user messages, optional replies
and plugin finalize decisions keep their existing behavior.

Adaptations for v2026.8.1:
- The NO_REPLY clause from upstream PR #164896 (v2026.10.1) is left out. v2026.8.1
  has no kept-answer delivery, so a silent follow-up could drop the reply that
  already reported the blocker.
- Any accepted sessions_spawn child counts as pending work. v2026.8.1 has no
  expectsCompletionMessage marker.
- The upstream steering-admission object does not exist here. A subscription
  that was unsubscribed during the finalize hook, or an attempt that no longer
  owns the active run, skips the check.
- Refusals are read from the provider_refusal diagnostic directly.
- deferTerminalDelivery keeps live assistant streaming unless a
  before_agent_finalize hook is registered. Without it, every run would buffer
  its assistant text until the end.
- LobsterAI addition: when the check continues the run, the runtime emits a
  `checkpoint` agent event after the finished answer is flushed. The desktop
  client closes that answer's segment on it, so a short answer followed by more
  text is not replaced by the follow-up.

Retire when the pinned upstream reaches v2026.10.1, which contains all three
upstream changes.

